course: dictionary
lesson: 2931
title: A drawl: slow and stretched
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A drawl is a slow way of speaking. When someone drawls, they stretch out the vowel sounds, so the words last longer. You can also use drawl as a verb: he drawled.
explain: The Mock Turtle's list uses sound-alike jokes: «Drawling (drawing)». Drawling sounds like drawing, but it means something different. The joke works because the two words sound the same. Read the words around a word to see what it means.
explain: In stories, «he drawled» tells you how someone spoke: lazily, bored or cocky. «A lazy drawl» suggests the speaker is relaxed, or not really trying. «A Southern drawl» is a drawl typical of parts of the southern USA.
fact: A drawl is a slow way of speaking, with the vowel sounds stretched out.
fact: «Drawled» is a verb, so you can say «he drawled» or «she drawled».
fact: «A Southern drawl» is a drawl typical of parts of the southern USA.
fact: «A lazy drawl» suggests the speaker is relaxed, bored or cocky.
fact: In the Mock Turtle's list, «Drawling (drawing)» is a sound-alike joke: the words sound the same but mean different things.
exercise: What does a drawl mean? | To shout very loudly | *A slow way of speaking, with the vowel sounds stretched out | To write in pencil | To run very fast
exercise: Why is «Drawling (drawing)» a joke in the Mock Turtle's list? | *The two words sound alike and the joke works because of it | The two words sound alike but mean different things | The two words are both verbs about running | The two words are spelled in the same way
exercise: What does «a lazy drawl» suggest? | *Relaxed or bored talking | Very fast, angry shouting | Singing in a choir | Whispering in a library
test: Which phrase means a slow, stretched way of speaking typical of parts of the USA? | a loud shout | a silent pause | *a Southern drawl | a quick whisper
test: In «he drawled», what kind of word is drawled? | an adjective | *a verb | a pronoun | a noun
exam: Which word in the Mock Turtle's list is the sound-alike joke for drawing? | Stretching | *Drawling | Mystery | Seaography
